On Monday, August 5, 2013 10:54:10 AM UTC+4, la arxokuna wrote:
>
> A new forum tool is added.
>
> http://mw.lojban.org/index.php/Special:AWCforum/
>
> e-mail notifications are working.
> In order to create an avatar upload an image using normal mediawiki upload 
> tool (http://mw.lojban.org/index.php/Special:Upload) and then opening 
> http://mw.lojban.org/index.php/Special:AWCforum/member_options/editava
>
> and pasting the name of your file in [[File: ..... . jpg]] format.
>
> Some features are not working. And won't work as the extension is quite 
> old there are no other good forum extensions for mediawiki.
>
> You can see some lojbanists already adding topic there.
>

1. LMW upgraded to bleeding edge nightly MediaWiki 1.22 wmf11.
2. I fixed AWC forum extension and viewing user profiles in it now works. 
AWC extension now works for this MW 1.22 wmf11

3. *And now the great news. Thanks to banseljaj VisualEditor+Parsoid now 
works. This extension transforms the wiki into a Microsoft Word (or 
LibreOffice Writer)-like editor. Now you don't have to know mediawiki 
syntax. Just click on "Edit" and start visually editing pages. Even if you 
are a n00b.*
*
*
*As you can see MediaWiki is now much better than the old Tiki.*
*
*
Of course the content is to be improved and improved but from technical 
side everything is perfect. Or almost perfect :P

Isn't it time to start contributing NOW ?

P.S. Any feedback is welcomed.

